import Polyfold.Chapter2.Retracts

/-!
Hofer–Wysocki–Zehnder, *Polyfold and Fredholm Theory I* (2014 preprint), Part I, §2.2,
Definitions 2.11–2.14, the filtration `X_m` and Lemma 2.3.9 (preprint 2.15), Definition 2.3.18 (preprint 2.20).

# M-polyfolds

## The text, paraphrased

(Definition 2.3.2 (preprint 2.11)) A chart around `x` in a topological space `X` is `(V, φ, (O, C, E))`: `V` an
open neighbourhood of `x`, `φ : V → O` a homeomorphism onto an sc-smooth retract `(O, C, E)`.  Two
charts are sc-smoothly compatible if the transition maps `ψ ∘ φ⁻¹ : φ(V ∩ V') → ψ(V ∩ V')` and
`φ ∘ ψ⁻¹` are sc-smooth between the retracts `(φ(V ∩ V'), C, E)` and `(ψ(V ∩ V'), C', E')`
(Proposition 2.3.1 (preprint 2.10) (1)).  (Definition 2.3.3 (preprint 2.12)) An sc-smooth atlas is a set of pairwise compatible
charts whose domains cover `X`; two atlases are equivalent if their union is an atlas.
(Definition 2.3.4 (preprint 2.13)) An M-polyfold is a Hausdorff paracompact space with an equivalence class of
sc-smooth atlases.  (Definition 2.3.8 (preprint 2.14)) `f : X → Y` is sc-smooth if for charts `φ` around `x`,
`φ'` around `f(x)` with `f(V) ⊆ V'`, `φ' ∘ f ∘ φ⁻¹ : O → O'` is sc-smooth in the sense of
Definition 2.1.14 (preprint 2.7); "the definition does not depend on the choice of sc-smoothly compatible charts".
A point `x` is on level `m` if `φ(x) ∈ O_m` for a chart around `x` ("independent of the chart");
`X_m` is the set of these points, with the topology generated by the sets `φ⁻¹(W)`, `W` open in
`O_m`; `X = X₀ ⊃ X₁ ⊃ ⋯ ⊃ X_∞ = ⋂ X_m`.  (Lemma 2.3.9 (preprint 2.15)) The inclusion `X_{m+1} → X_m` is continuous.
(Theorem 2.3.10 (preprint 2.16)) Every `X_m` and `X_∞` is metrizable (Appendix 2.6.2, by Smirnov's theorem).
(Definition 2.3.18 (preprint 2.20)) `A ⊆ X` is a sub-M-polyfold if every `a ∈ A` has an open neighbourhood `V` and
an sc-smooth retraction `r : V → V` with `r(V) = A ∩ V`.

## What is formalized

* `Polyfold.MChart X` (**Definition 2.3.2 (preprint 2.11)**): a local model `(O, C, E)`, a `PartialEquiv X E₀` with
  open source and target `O`, continuous in both directions.  `MChart.overlap φ ψ = φ(V ∩ V')`,
  which is an open subset of `O` and hence a retract (`MChart.isScRetract_overlap`);
  `MChart.transition φ ψ = ψ ∘ φ⁻¹`; `MChart.Compatible φ ψ`.
* `MChart.compatible_of_locally`: if `φ` and `ψ` are each compatible with the charts of a family
  covering `V ∩ V'`, they are compatible with each other (the chain rule, Theorem 2.1.15 (preprint 2.8), together
  with the locality of sc-smoothness).  This is what makes the maximal atlas work.
* `Polyfold.MAtlas X` (**Definition 2.3.3 (preprint 2.12)**), `MAtlas.Equiv` ("the union is an atlas",
  `MAtlas.equiv_iff`), `Polyfold.MPolyfold X` (**Definition 2.3.4 (preprint 2.13)**, for `X` Hausdorff and
  paracompact, given by an atlas; `MPolyfold.IsChart` is the maximal atlas, which depends only on
  the equivalence class: `MPolyfold.isChart_congr`).
* `MPolyfold.levelSet P m` (`X_m`), `MPolyfold.mem_levelSet_iff` (independence of the chart),
  `MPolyfold.smoothSet` (`X_∞`), `MPolyfold.levelTopology` (the topology on `X_m` generated by the
  text's sets), and `Polyfold.lemma_2_3_9` (**Lemma 2.3.9 (preprint 2.15)**).
* `Polyfold.MPolyfold.IsScSmoothOn P Q f U` and `MPolyfold.IsScSmoothMap` (**Definition 2.3.8 (preprint 2.14)**),
  with `IsScSmoothOn.comp` (compositions) and `isScSmoothMap_id`.
* `Polyfold.MPolyfold.IsSubMPolyfold P A` (**Definition 2.3.18 (preprint 2.20)**).
* `Polyfold.LocalModel.toMPolyfold`: a nonempty sc-smooth retract `O` is an M-polyfold with the
  single chart `id : O → O` (the text's "a retract `O` is an M-polyfold", before Theorem 2.4.12 (preprint 2.31)).

## What the text leaves implicit, and the choices made

* "An equivalence class of atlases" is represented by one atlas; every notion defined afterwards is
  defined through the *maximal* atlas `IsChart` (all charts compatible with the given atlas), which
  is the same for equivalent atlases (`isChart_congr`).  For this, charts compatible with an atlas
  must be compatible with each other (`IsChart.compatible`), which the text does not discuss; the
  proof needs that sc-smoothness between retracts is local (`IsScSmoothRetractMap.of_locally`).
* Definition 2.3.8 (preprint 2.14) is read with all charts of the maximal atlases: for every chart `φ` of `X`,
  `ψ` of `Y`, and every open `V ⊆ U ∩ dom φ` with `f(V) ⊆ dom ψ`, the map `ψ ∘ f ∘ φ⁻¹` is sc-smooth
  on the retract `(φ(V), C, E)`.  The text's "charts around `x` with `f(V) ⊆ V'`" presupposes that
  such pairs exist around every point, which is the continuity of `f`; continuity is therefore a
  field (`continuousOn`), and the open set `U` on which `f` is considered is a parameter (the text
  only has `U = X`, but germs and sub-M-polyfolds need open subsets).
* The topology on `X_m` is defined as generated by the text's family `B`; that `B` is a basis
  (closed under intersections) is not needed and not proved.  Theorem 2.3.10 (preprint 2.16) (`X`, every `X_m` and
  `X_∞` metrizable, every `X_m` paracompact) is `Polyfold.theorem_2_3_10` in `Metrizable.lean`, with
  no added hypothesis; Smirnov's theorem, which is not in Mathlib, is proved there
  (`Polyfold.metrizableSpace_of_locally`).  That `(V_m, φ, (O_m, C_m, E_m))` are charts making
  `X_m` an M-polyfold is proved for `m = 1` in `LevelPolyfold.lean` (`MPolyfold.shift`, through
  Proposition 1.2.2 (preprint 1.17) for retracts, `IsScSmoothRetractMap.shift`); for `m ≥ 2` it is not formalized
  (gap G.6 of the report).
* The tangent bundle `TX` (Definitions 2.17–2.18, Proposition 2.3.15 (preprint 2.19) (1), continuity in (2), `TX`
  as an M-polyfold) is in `TangentBundle.lean`, Proposition 2.3.15 (preprint 2.19) (3) (`Polyfold.proposition_2_3_15_three`)
  in `Metrizable.lean`.  Proposition 2.3.19 (preprint 2.21) (the structure, (1), (2)) is in `SubMPolyfold.lean`;
  (3), (4) are proved in a chart (`Polyfold.proposition_2_3_19_three`, `Polyfold.proposition_2_3_19_four`) in
  `Metrizable.lean`.  Not formalized: the linear and sc-structures of `T_xX`, hence 2.21 (3), (4)
  in `T_aX` (G.7), and the openness of `p : TX → X_1` in Proposition 2.3.15 (preprint 2.19) (2) (G.8).
-/

open Set Filter Topology Function

noncomputable section

namespace Polyfold

universe u v w

/-! ### Charts (Definition 2.3.2 (preprint 2.11)) -/

/-- An **M-polyfold chart** on a topological space `X` (Definition 2.3.2 (preprint 2.11)): a local model
`(O, C, E)` and a homeomorphism `φ : V → O` from an open set `V ⊆ X` onto `O`, as a partial
equivalence `X ≃ E₀` with source `V` and target `O`. -/
structure MChart (X : Type u) [TopologicalSpace X] where
  /-- The local model `(O, C, E)`. -/
  model : LocalModel
  /-- The chart map `φ`, with its inverse. -/
  toPartialEquiv : PartialEquiv X (model.E 0)
  isOpen_source : IsOpen toPartialEquiv.source
  target_eq : toPartialEquiv.target = model.O
  continuousOn_toFun : ContinuousOn toPartialEquiv toPartialEquiv.source
  continuousOn_invFun : ContinuousOn toPartialEquiv.symm model.O

namespace MChart

variable {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X] (φ ψ χ : MChart X)

instance : CoeFun (MChart X) (fun φ => X → φ.model.E 0) := ⟨fun φ => φ.toPartialEquiv⟩

/-- The domain `V` of the chart. -/
abbrev source : Set X := φ.toPartialEquiv.source

/-- The inverse `φ⁻¹ : E₀ → X` (a total function; meaningful on `O`). -/
abbrev symm : φ.model.E 0 → X := φ.toPartialEquiv.symm

lemma mapsTo_model (x : X) (hx : x ∈ φ.source) : φ x ∈ φ.model.O :=
  φ.target_eq ▸ φ.toPartialEquiv.map_source hx

lemma symm_mapsTo {z : φ.model.E 0} (hz : z ∈ φ.model.O) : φ.symm z ∈ φ.source :=
  φ.toPartialEquiv.map_target (φ.target_eq ▸ hz)

lemma symm_apply_apply {x : X} (hx : x ∈ φ.source) : φ.symm (φ x) = x :=
  φ.toPartialEquiv.left_inv hx

lemma apply_symm_apply {z : φ.model.E 0} (hz : z ∈ φ.model.O) : φ (φ.symm z) = z :=
  φ.toPartialEquiv.right_inv (φ.target_eq ▸ hz)

lemma image_source : φ '' φ.source = φ.model.O :=
  φ.toPartialEquiv.image_source_eq_target.trans φ.target_eq

lemma image_subset_model {s : Set X} (hs : s ⊆ φ.source) : φ '' s ⊆ φ.model.O :=
  (image_mono hs).trans φ.image_source.le

/-- The image of a subset of the source: `φ(s) = O ∩ (φ⁻¹)⁻¹(s)` for `s ⊆ V`. -/
lemma image_eq_inter_preimage_symm {s : Set X} (hs : s ⊆ φ.source) :
    φ '' s = φ.model.O ∩ φ.symm ⁻¹' s := by
  ext z
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨φ.mapsTo_model x (hs hx), by rw [mem_preimage, φ.symm_apply_apply (hs hx)]; exact hx⟩
  · rintro ⟨hz, hzs⟩
    exact ⟨φ.symm z, hzs, φ.apply_symm_apply hz⟩

/-- The image of an open subset of the source is an open subset of `O`. -/
lemma exists_isOpen_image_eq {s : Set X} (hs : s ⊆ φ.source) (hso : IsOpen s) :
    ∃ W : Set (φ.model.E 0), IsOpen W ∧ φ '' s = φ.model.O ∩ W := by
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hWs⟩ := (continuousOn_iff'.1 φ.continuousOn_invFun) s hso
  refine ⟨W, hW, ?_⟩
  rw [φ.image_eq_inter_preimage_symm hs, inter_comm, hWs, inter_comm]

/-- The image of an open subset of the source is an sc-smooth retract (Proposition 2.3.1 (preprint 2.10) (1)). -/
lemma isScRetract_image {s : Set X} (hs : s ⊆ φ.source) (hso : IsOpen s) :
    IsScRetract φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ '' s) := by
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hWs⟩ := φ.exists_isOpen_image_eq hs hso
  rw [hWs]
  exact proposition_2_3_1_one φ.model.isScRetract hW

/-- The restriction of a chart to an open subset `s` of its source. -/
def restrict {s : Set X} (hs : s ⊆ φ.source) (hso : IsOpen s) : MChart X where
  model := ⟨φ.model.E, φ.model.C, φ '' s, φ.isScRetract_image hs hso⟩
  toPartialEquiv := φ.toPartialEquiv.restr s |>.copy _ rfl _ rfl s (by
      rw [PartialEquiv.restr_source, inter_eq_right.2 hs]) (φ '' s)
      (by rw [PartialEquiv.restr_target, φ.image_eq_inter_preimage_symm hs, φ.target_eq])
  isOpen_source := hso
  target_eq := rfl
  continuousOn_toFun := φ.continuousOn_toFun.mono hs
  continuousOn_invFun := φ.continuousOn_invFun.mono (φ.image_subset_model hs)

@[simp] lemma restrict_source {s : Set X} (hs : s ⊆ φ.source) (hso : IsOpen s) :
    (φ.restrict hs hso).source = s := rfl

@[simp] lemma restrict_apply {s : Set X} (hs : s ⊆ φ.source) (hso : IsOpen s) (x : X) :
    φ.restrict hs hso x = φ x := rfl

@[simp] lemma restrict_symm_apply {s : Set X} (hs : s ⊆ φ.source) (hso : IsOpen s)
    (z : φ.model.E 0) : (φ.restrict hs hso).symm z = φ.symm z := rfl

@[simp] lemma restrict_model_O {s : Set X} (hs : s ⊆ φ.source) (hso : IsOpen s) :
    (φ.restrict hs hso).model.O = φ '' s := rfl

/-! ### Transition maps and compatibility -/

/-- The overlap `φ(V ∩ V')` of two charts, seen in the first chart. -/
def overlap : Set (φ.model.E 0) := φ '' (φ.source ∩ ψ.source)

lemma overlap_subset : φ.overlap ψ ⊆ φ.model.O := φ.image_subset_model inter_subset_left

lemma isScRetract_overlap : IsScRetract φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ.overlap ψ) :=
  φ.isScRetract_image inter_subset_left (φ.isOpen_source.inter ψ.isOpen_source)

lemma mem_overlap {x : X} (hx : x ∈ φ.source) (hx' : x ∈ ψ.source) : φ x ∈ φ.overlap ψ :=
  ⟨x, ⟨hx, hx'⟩, rfl⟩

/-- The transition map `ψ ∘ φ⁻¹`, as a total function `E₀ → E'₀`. -/
def transition : φ.model.E 0 → ψ.model.E 0 := ψ ∘ φ.symm

lemma transition_apply {x : X} (hx : x ∈ φ.source) : φ.transition ψ (φ x) = ψ x := by
  simp only [transition, Function.comp_apply, φ.symm_apply_apply hx]

lemma transition_mapsTo : MapsTo (φ.transition ψ) (φ.overlap ψ) (ψ.overlap φ) := by
  rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
  rw [φ.transition_apply ψ hx.1]
  exact ⟨x, ⟨hx.2, hx.1⟩, rfl⟩

/-- **Definition 2.3.2 (preprint 2.11)**: two charts are **sc-smoothly compatible** if both transition maps are
sc-smooth between the overlap retracts. -/
def Compatible : Prop :=
  IsScSmoothRetractMap φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ.overlap ψ) ψ.model.E ψ.model.C (ψ.overlap φ)
      (φ.transition ψ) ∧
    IsScSmoothRetractMap ψ.model.E ψ.model.C (ψ.overlap φ) φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ.overlap ψ)
      (ψ.transition φ)

variable {φ ψ} in
lemma Compatible.symm (h : φ.Compatible ψ) : ψ.Compatible φ := ⟨h.2, h.1⟩

/-- `A ∩ W = O ∩ W` when `A ⊆ O` and `O ∩ W ⊆ A`. -/
lemma _root_.Polyfold.inter_eq_inter_of_subset {α : Type*} {A O W : Set α} (hAO : A ⊆ O)
    (hOW : O ∩ W ⊆ A) : A ∩ W = O ∩ W :=
  Subset.antisymm (inter_subset_inter_left _ hAO) fun _ hz => ⟨hOW hz, hz.2⟩

/-- A chart is compatible with itself. -/
lemma compatible_self : φ.Compatible φ := by
  have h : IsScSmoothRetractMap φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ.overlap φ) φ.model.E φ.model.C
      (φ.overlap φ) (φ.transition φ) := by
    refine (isScSmoothRetractMap_id _).congr ?_
    rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    rw [id, φ.transition_apply φ hx.1]
  exact ⟨h, h⟩

/-- The image `φ(s ∩ V')` of a subset `s ⊆ V` is `φ(V ∩ V') ∩ W` for an open `W`. -/
lemma overlap_restrict_eq {s : Set X} (hs : s ⊆ φ.source) (hso : IsOpen s) :
    ∃ W : Set (φ.model.E 0), IsOpen W ∧ (φ.restrict hs hso).overlap ψ = φ.overlap ψ ∩ W := by
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hWeq⟩ := φ.exists_isOpen_image_eq (s := s ∩ ψ.source)
    (inter_subset_left.trans hs) (hso.inter ψ.isOpen_source)
  refine ⟨W, hW, ?_⟩
  change φ '' (s ∩ ψ.source) = φ.overlap ψ ∩ W
  rw [hWeq]
  ext z
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨hz, hzW⟩
    refine ⟨?_, hzW⟩
    have : z ∈ φ '' (s ∩ ψ.source) := by rw [hWeq]; exact ⟨hz, hzW⟩
    obtain ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ := this
    exact ⟨x, ⟨hs hx.1, hx.2⟩, rfl⟩
  · rintro ⟨hz, hzW⟩
    exact ⟨φ.overlap_subset ψ hz, hzW⟩

variable {φ ψ} in
/-- Compatibility passes to the restriction of the first chart. -/
lemma Compatible.restrict_left (h : φ.Compatible ψ) {s : Set X} (hs : s ⊆ φ.source)
    (hso : IsOpen s) : (φ.restrict hs hso).Compatible ψ := by
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hWeq⟩ := φ.overlap_restrict_eq ψ hs hso
  constructor
  · rw [hWeq]
    refine (h.1.restrict (φ.isScRetract_overlap ψ)).mono_target ?_
    rw [← hWeq]
    exact (φ.restrict hs hso).transition_mapsTo ψ
  · -- the other direction: `φ ∘ ψ⁻¹` on `ψ(V' ∩ s) = ψ(V' ∩ V) ∩ W'`
    obtain ⟨W', hW', hW'eq⟩ := ψ.exists_isOpen_image_eq (s := ψ.source ∩ s)
      inter_subset_left (ψ.isOpen_source.inter hso)
    have hover : ψ.overlap (φ.restrict hs hso) = ψ.overlap φ ∩ W' := by
      change ψ '' (ψ.source ∩ s) = ψ.overlap φ ∩ W'
      rw [hW'eq]
      ext z
      constructor
      · rintro ⟨hz, hzW⟩
        refine ⟨?_, hzW⟩
        have : z ∈ ψ '' (ψ.source ∩ s) := by rw [hW'eq]; exact ⟨hz, hzW⟩
        obtain ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ := this
        exact ⟨x, ⟨hx.1, hs hx.2⟩, rfl⟩
      · rintro ⟨hz, hzW⟩
        exact ⟨ψ.overlap_subset φ hz, hzW⟩
    rw [hover]
    refine (h.2.restrict (ψ.isScRetract_overlap φ)).mono_target ?_
    rw [← hover]
    exact ψ.transition_mapsTo (φ.restrict hs hso)

variable {φ ψ} in
lemma Compatible.restrict_right (h : φ.Compatible ψ) {t : Set X} (ht : t ⊆ ψ.source)
    (hto : IsOpen t) : φ.Compatible (ψ.restrict ht hto) :=
  (h.symm.restrict_left ht hto).symm

variable {φ ψ} in
/-- Compatibility passes to restrictions of both charts. -/
lemma Compatible.restrict (h : φ.Compatible ψ) {s : Set X} (hs : s ⊆ φ.source) (hso : IsOpen s)
    {t : Set X} (ht : t ⊆ ψ.source) (hto : IsOpen t) :
    (φ.restrict hs hso).Compatible (ψ.restrict ht hto) :=
  (h.restrict_left hs hso).restrict_right ht hto

/-- The transition map `ψ ∘ φ⁻¹` factors through a third chart `χ` on `φ(V ∩ V' ∩ V'')`. -/
lemma transition_eq_comp_on {x : X} (hx : x ∈ φ.source) (hx'' : x ∈ χ.source) :
    φ.transition ψ (φ x) = χ.transition ψ (φ.transition χ (φ x)) := by
  rw [φ.transition_apply ψ hx, φ.transition_apply χ hx, χ.transition_apply ψ hx'']

/-- **Compatibility is local**: if `φ` and `ψ` are compatible with every chart of a family `S`
whose domains cover `V ∩ V'`, then `φ` and `ψ` are compatible.  (Chain rule and locality.) -/
theorem compatible_of_locally (S : Set (MChart X)) (hφ : ∀ χ ∈ S, φ.Compatible χ)
    (hψ : ∀ χ ∈ S, χ.Compatible ψ)
    (hcover : ∀ x ∈ φ.source ∩ ψ.source, ∃ χ ∈ S, x ∈ χ.source) : φ.Compatible ψ := by
  -- one direction, then apply it twice
  have key : ∀ (φ ψ : MChart X), (∀ χ ∈ S, φ.Compatible χ) → (∀ χ ∈ S, χ.Compatible ψ) →
      (∀ x ∈ φ.source ∩ ψ.source, ∃ χ ∈ S, x ∈ χ.source) →
      IsScSmoothRetractMap φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ.overlap ψ) ψ.model.E ψ.model.C (ψ.overlap φ)
        (φ.transition ψ) := by
    intro φ ψ hφ hψ hcover
    refine IsScSmoothRetractMap.of_locally (φ.transition_mapsTo ψ) ?_
    rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨χ, hχS, hxχ⟩ := hcover x hx
    -- the open set `s = V ∩ V' ∩ V''` and its image `φ(s) = O ∩ W`
    set s := φ.source ∩ ψ.source ∩ χ.source with hs
    have hso : IsOpen s := (φ.isOpen_source.inter ψ.isOpen_source).inter χ.isOpen_source
    have hsφ : s ⊆ φ.source := fun y hy => hy.1.1
    obtain ⟨W, hW, hWeq⟩ := φ.exists_isOpen_image_eq hsφ hso
    refine ⟨W, hW, ?_, ?_⟩
    · have : φ x ∈ φ '' s := ⟨x, ⟨hx, hxχ⟩, rfl⟩
      rw [hWeq] at this; exact this.2
    · have hover : φ.overlap ψ ∩ W = φ '' s := by
        rw [hWeq]
        exact inter_eq_inter_of_subset (φ.overlap_subset ψ)
          (hWeq ▸ image_mono fun y hy => ⟨hy.1.1, hy.1.2⟩)
      rw [hover]
      -- `ψ ∘ φ⁻¹ = (ψ ∘ χ⁻¹) ∘ (χ ∘ φ⁻¹)` on `φ(s)`
      have h1 : IsScSmoothRetractMap φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ '' s) χ.model.E χ.model.C (χ '' s)
          (φ.transition χ) := by
        have := (hφ χ hχS).1.restrict (φ.isScRetract_overlap χ) (W := W)
        have hover' : φ.overlap χ ∩ W = φ '' s := by
          rw [hWeq]
          exact inter_eq_inter_of_subset (φ.overlap_subset χ)
            (hWeq ▸ image_mono fun y hy => ⟨hy.1.1, hy.2⟩)
        rw [hover'] at this
        refine this.mono_target ?_
        rintro _ ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
        rw [φ.transition_apply χ hy.1.1]
        exact ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
      have h2 : IsScSmoothRetractMap χ.model.E χ.model.C (χ '' s) ψ.model.E ψ.model.C
          (ψ.overlap φ) (χ.transition ψ) := by
        have hsχ : s ⊆ χ.source := fun y hy => hy.2
        obtain ⟨W', hW', hW'eq⟩ := χ.exists_isOpen_image_eq hsχ hso
        have := (hψ χ hχS).1.restrict (χ.isScRetract_overlap ψ) (W := W')
        have hover' : χ.overlap ψ ∩ W' = χ '' s := by
          rw [hW'eq]
          exact inter_eq_inter_of_subset (χ.overlap_subset ψ)
            (hW'eq ▸ image_mono fun y hy => ⟨hy.2, hy.1.2⟩)
        rw [hover'] at this
        refine this.mono_target ?_
        rintro _ ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
        rw [χ.transition_apply ψ hy.2]
        exact ⟨y, ⟨hy.1.2, hy.1.1⟩, rfl⟩
      have hχs : IsScRetract χ.model.E χ.model.C (χ '' s) :=
        χ.isScRetract_image (fun y hy => hy.2) hso
      refine (h2.comp h1 hχs).congr ?_
      rintro _ ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
      exact (φ.transition_eq_comp_on ψ χ hy.1.1 hy.2).symm
  refine ⟨key φ ψ hφ hψ hcover, key ψ φ (fun χ hχ => (hψ χ hχ).symm) (fun χ hχ => (hφ χ hχ).symm) ?_⟩
  intro x hx
  exact hcover x ⟨hx.2, hx.1⟩

end MChart

/-! ### Atlases (Definition 2.3.3 (preprint 2.12)) and M-polyfolds (Definition 2.3.4 (preprint 2.13)) -/

/-- An **sc-smooth atlas** (Definition 2.3.3 (preprint 2.12)): pairwise compatible charts covering `X`. -/
structure MAtlas (X : Type u) [TopologicalSpace X] where
  charts : Set (MChart X)
  compatible : ∀ φ ∈ charts, ∀ ψ ∈ charts, φ.Compatible ψ
  cover : ∀ x : X, ∃ φ ∈ charts, x ∈ φ.source

namespace MAtlas

variable {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X]

/-- **Definition 2.3.3 (preprint 2.12)**: two atlases are **equivalent** if their union is an atlas. -/
def Equiv (A B : MAtlas X) : Prop := ∃ D : MAtlas X, D.charts = A.charts ∪ B.charts

/-- Equivalence of atlases is pairwise compatibility of their charts. -/
theorem equiv_iff (A B : MAtlas X) :
    A.Equiv B ↔ ∀ φ ∈ A.charts, ∀ ψ ∈ B.charts, φ.Compatible ψ := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨D, hD⟩ φ hφ ψ hψ
    exact D.compatible φ (hD ▸ Or.inl hφ) ψ (hD ▸ Or.inr hψ)
  · intro h
    refine ⟨⟨A.charts ∪ B.charts, ?_, fun x => ?_⟩, rfl⟩
    · rintro φ (hφ | hφ) ψ (hψ | hψ)
      · exact A.compatible φ hφ ψ hψ
      · exact h φ hφ ψ hψ
      · exact (h ψ hψ φ hφ).symm
      · exact B.compatible φ hφ ψ hψ
    · obtain ⟨φ, hφ, hx⟩ := A.cover x
      exact ⟨φ, Or.inl hφ, hx⟩

lemma Equiv.refl (A : MAtlas X) : A.Equiv A := ⟨A, (union_self _).symm⟩

lemma Equiv.symm {A B : MAtlas X} (h : A.Equiv B) : B.Equiv A := by
  obtain ⟨D, hD⟩ := h
  exact ⟨D, hD.trans (union_comm _ _)⟩

end MAtlas

/-- An **M-polyfold** (Definition 2.3.4 (preprint 2.13)): a Hausdorff paracompact topological space with an
sc-smooth atlas (representing its equivalence class; see `MPolyfold.IsChart`). -/
structure MPolyfold (X : Type u) [TopologicalSpace X] [T2Space X] [ParacompactSpace X] where
  atlas : MAtlas X

namespace MPolyfold

variable {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X] [T2Space X] [ParacompactSpace X] (P : MPolyfold X)

/-- The charts of the M-polyfold structure: all charts compatible with the given atlas (the
maximal atlas of the equivalence class). -/
def IsChart (φ : MChart X) : Prop := ∀ ψ ∈ P.atlas.charts, φ.Compatible ψ

lemma isChart_of_mem {φ : MChart X} (hφ : φ ∈ P.atlas.charts) : P.IsChart φ :=
  fun ψ hψ => P.atlas.compatible φ hφ ψ hψ

/-- Two charts of the structure are compatible (by the locality of compatibility). -/
theorem IsChart.compatible {φ ψ : MChart X} (hφ : P.IsChart φ) (hψ : P.IsChart ψ) :
    φ.Compatible ψ :=
  MChart.compatible_of_locally φ ψ P.atlas.charts hφ (fun χ hχ => (hψ χ hχ).symm)
    fun x _ => P.atlas.cover x

/-- The restriction of a chart of the structure to an open subset of its source. -/
theorem IsChart.restrict {φ : MChart X} (hφ : P.IsChart φ) {s : Set X} (hs : s ⊆ φ.source)
    (hso : IsOpen s) : P.IsChart (φ.restrict hs hso) :=
  fun ψ hψ => (hφ ψ hψ).restrict_left hs hso

/-- The maximal atlas depends only on the equivalence class of the atlas. -/
theorem isChart_congr {P Q : MPolyfold X} (h : P.atlas.Equiv Q.atlas) (φ : MChart X) :
    P.IsChart φ ↔ Q.IsChart φ := by
  rw [MAtlas.equiv_iff] at h
  constructor
  · intro hφ ψ hψ
    exact MChart.compatible_of_locally φ ψ P.atlas.charts hφ (fun χ hχ => h χ hχ ψ hψ)
      fun x _ => P.atlas.cover x
  · intro hφ ψ hψ
    exact MChart.compatible_of_locally φ ψ Q.atlas.charts hφ (fun χ hχ => (h ψ hψ χ hχ).symm)
      fun x _ => Q.atlas.cover x

/-- Every point lies in the source of a chart of the structure. -/
lemma exists_isChart_mem_source (x : X) : ∃ φ : MChart X, P.IsChart φ ∧ x ∈ φ.source := by
  obtain ⟨φ, hφ, hx⟩ := P.atlas.cover x
  exact ⟨φ, P.isChart_of_mem hφ, hx⟩

/-! ### The filtration `X_m` and Lemma 2.3.9 (preprint 2.15) -/

/-- `X_m`, the points on level `m`: `φ(x) ∈ O_m = O ∩ E_m` for a chart `φ` around `x`.  Independent
of the chart (`mem_levelSet_iff`). -/
def levelSet (m : ℕ) : Set X :=
  {x | ∃ φ : MChart X, P.IsChart φ ∧ x ∈ φ.source ∧ φ x ∈ range (φ.model.E.toBase m)}

/-- Being on level `m` can be tested in any chart around the point (the text's "of course, this
definition is independent of the choice of a chart"). -/
theorem mem_levelSet_iff {m : ℕ} {φ : MChart X} (hφ : P.IsChart φ) {x : X} (hx : x ∈ φ.source) :
    x ∈ P.levelSet m ↔ φ x ∈ range (φ.model.E.toBase m) := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨ψ, hψ, hxψ, hψm⟩
    have hcomp := (hψ.compatible hφ (P := P)).1
    have := hcomp.mem_range_toBase (ψ.isScRetract_overlap φ) (ψ.mem_overlap φ hxψ hx) hψm
    rwa [ψ.transition_apply φ hxψ] at this
  · intro h
    exact ⟨φ, hφ, hx, h⟩

lemma levelSet_zero : P.levelSet 0 = univ := by
  refine eq_univ_of_forall fun x => ?_
  obtain ⟨φ, hφ, hx⟩ := P.exists_isChart_mem_source x
  exact ⟨φ, hφ, hx, ⟨φ x, rfl⟩⟩

/-- `X_{m+1} ⊆ X_m`. -/
lemma levelSet_succ_subset (m : ℕ) : P.levelSet (m + 1) ⊆ P.levelSet m := by
  rintro x ⟨φ, hφ, hx, z, hz⟩
  exact ⟨φ, hφ, hx, φ.model.E.incl m z, hz⟩

lemma levelSet_antitone : Antitone P.levelSet :=
  antitone_nat_of_succ_le P.levelSet_succ_subset

/-- `X_∞ = ⋂ X_m`, the smooth points. -/
def smoothSet : Set X := ⋂ m, P.levelSet m

/-- The lift of `φ(x)` to `E_m` (meaningful for `x ∈ V_m`). -/
def levelLift (φ : MChart X) (m : ℕ) (x : X) : φ.model.E m :=
  Function.invFun (φ.model.E.toBase m) (φ x)

lemma toBase_levelLift {m : ℕ} {φ : MChart X} (hφ : P.IsChart φ) {x : X} (hx : x ∈ φ.source)
    (hxm : x ∈ P.levelSet m) : φ.model.E.toBase m (levelLift φ m x) = φ x :=
  Function.invFun_eq ((P.mem_levelSet_iff hφ hx).1 hxm)

/-- The lift to `E_m` is the inclusion of the lift to `E_{m+1}`. -/
lemma levelLift_eq_incl {m : ℕ} {φ : MChart X} (hφ : P.IsChart φ) {x : X} (hx : x ∈ φ.source)
    (hxm : x ∈ P.levelSet (m + 1)) :
    levelLift φ m x = φ.model.E.incl m (levelLift φ (m + 1) x) := by
  apply φ.model.E.toBase_injective m
  rw [← ScScale.toBase_succ, P.toBase_levelLift hφ hx hxm,
    P.toBase_levelLift hφ hx (P.levelSet_succ_subset m hxm)]

/-- The text's family `B` of subsets of `X_m`: `φ⁻¹(W)` for a chart `φ` and `W` open in `O_m`
(given as `W' ∩ O_m` with `W'` open in `E_m`). -/
def levelBasis (m : ℕ) : Set (Set (P.levelSet m)) :=
  {s | ∃ (φ : MChart X) (_ : P.IsChart φ) (W : Set (φ.model.E m)), IsOpen W ∧
    s = {x : P.levelSet m | (x : X) ∈ φ.source ∧ levelLift φ m (x : X) ∈ W}}

/-- The topology on `X_m` generated by `B`. -/
@[instance_reducible] def levelTopology (m : ℕ) : TopologicalSpace (P.levelSet m) :=
  TopologicalSpace.generateFrom (P.levelBasis m)

/-- The inclusion `X_{m+1} → X_m`. -/
def levelIncl (m : ℕ) : P.levelSet (m + 1) → P.levelSet m :=
  fun x => ⟨x, P.levelSet_succ_subset m x.2⟩

/-- **Lemma 2.3.9 (preprint 2.15)**: the inclusion `X_{m+1} → X_m` is continuous. -/
theorem _root_.Polyfold.lemma_2_3_9 (m : ℕ) :
    @Continuous _ _ (P.levelTopology (m + 1)) (P.levelTopology m) (P.levelIncl m) := by
  change @Continuous _ _ (TopologicalSpace.generateFrom (P.levelBasis (m + 1)))
    (TopologicalSpace.generateFrom (P.levelBasis m)) (P.levelIncl m)
  rw [continuous_generateFrom_iff]
  rintro s ⟨φ, hφ, W, hW, rfl⟩
  apply TopologicalSpace.isOpen_generateFrom_of_mem
  refine ⟨φ, hφ, φ.model.E.incl m ⁻¹' W, hW.preimage (φ.model.E.incl m).continuous, ?_⟩
  ext x
  change ((x : X) ∈ φ.source ∧ levelLift φ m (x : X) ∈ W) ↔
    (x : X) ∈ φ.source ∧ φ.model.E.incl m (levelLift φ (m + 1) (x : X)) ∈ W
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨hx, hxW⟩
    exact ⟨hx, by rwa [← P.levelLift_eq_incl hφ hx x.2]⟩
  · rintro ⟨hx, hxW⟩
    exact ⟨hx, by rwa [P.levelLift_eq_incl hφ hx x.2]⟩

/-! ### Sc-smooth maps between M-polyfolds (Definition 2.3.8 (preprint 2.14)) -/

variable {Y : Type v} [TopologicalSpace Y] [T2Space Y] [ParacompactSpace Y] (Q : MPolyfold Y)
  {Z : Type w} [TopologicalSpace Z] [T2Space Z] [ParacompactSpace Z] (S : MPolyfold Z)

/-- **Definition 2.3.8 (preprint 2.14)**: `f : X → Y` is **sc-smooth on the open set `U`** if it is continuous on
`U` and, for all charts `φ` of `X` and `ψ` of `Y` and every open `V ⊆ U ∩ dom φ` with
`f(V) ⊆ dom ψ`, the coordinate representation `ψ ∘ f ∘ φ⁻¹` is sc-smooth between the retracts
`(φ(V), C, E)` and `(O', C', E')`. -/
structure IsScSmoothOn (f : X → Y) (U : Set X) : Prop where
  isOpen : IsOpen U
  continuousOn : ContinuousOn f U
  smooth : ∀ (φ : MChart X) (ψ : MChart Y), P.IsChart φ → Q.IsChart ψ →
    ∀ V : Set X, IsOpen V → V ⊆ U ∩ φ.source → MapsTo f V ψ.source →
      IsScSmoothRetractMap φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ '' V) ψ.model.E ψ.model.C ψ.model.O
        (ψ ∘ f ∘ φ.symm)

/-- **Definition 2.3.8 (preprint 2.14)**: an **sc-smooth map** `f : X → Y` between M-polyfolds. -/
def IsScSmoothMap (f : X → Y) : Prop := P.IsScSmoothOn Q f univ

variable {P Q S}

lemma IsScSmoothOn.mono {f : X → Y} {U U' : Set X} (h : P.IsScSmoothOn Q f U) (hU' : IsOpen U')
    (hsub : U' ⊆ U) : P.IsScSmoothOn Q f U' where
  isOpen := hU'
  continuousOn := h.continuousOn.mono hsub
  smooth φ ψ hφ hψ V hV hVU hfV :=
    h.smooth φ ψ hφ hψ V hV (hVU.trans (inter_subset_inter_left _ hsub)) hfV

lemma IsScSmoothOn.congr {f f' : X → Y} {U : Set X} (h : P.IsScSmoothOn Q f U) (hff' : EqOn f f' U) :
    P.IsScSmoothOn Q f' U where
  isOpen := h.isOpen
  continuousOn := h.continuousOn.congr hff'.symm
  smooth φ ψ hφ hψ V hV hVU hfV := by
    have hfV' : MapsTo f V ψ.source := fun x hx => hff' (hVU hx).1 ▸ hfV hx
    refine (h.smooth φ ψ hφ hψ V hV hVU hfV').congr ?_
    rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    simp only [Function.comp_apply, φ.symm_apply_apply (hVU hx).2, hff' (hVU hx).1]

/-- The identity is sc-smooth. -/
theorem isScSmoothMap_id : P.IsScSmoothMap P id where
  isOpen := isOpen_univ
  continuousOn := continuousOn_id
  smooth φ ψ hφ hψ V hV hVU hfV := by
    -- `ψ ∘ φ⁻¹` on `φ(V) ⊆ φ(V ∩ V')`: a restriction of the transition map
    have hVφ : V ⊆ φ.source := fun x hx => (hVU hx).2
    obtain ⟨W, hW, hWeq⟩ := φ.exists_isOpen_image_eq hVφ hV
    have h1 := (hφ.compatible hψ (P := P)).1.restrict (φ.isScRetract_overlap ψ) (W := W)
    have hover : φ.overlap ψ ∩ W = φ '' V := by
      rw [hWeq]
      ext z
      constructor
      · rintro ⟨hz, hzW⟩
        exact ⟨φ.overlap_subset ψ hz, hzW⟩
      · rintro ⟨hz, hzW⟩
        refine ⟨?_, hzW⟩
        have : z ∈ φ '' V := by rw [hWeq]; exact ⟨hz, hzW⟩
        obtain ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ := this
        exact ⟨x, ⟨hVφ hx, hfV hx⟩, rfl⟩
    rw [hover] at h1
    refine h1.mono_target ?_
    rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    change ψ (φ.symm (φ x)) ∈ ψ.model.O
    rw [φ.symm_apply_apply (hVφ hx)]
    exact ψ.mapsTo_model x (hfV hx)

/-- Compositions of sc-smooth maps are sc-smooth (Definition 2.3.8 (preprint 2.14) and Theorem 2.1.15 (preprint 2.8)). -/
theorem IsScSmoothOn.comp {f : X → Y} {g : Y → Z} {U : Set X} {U' : Set Y}
    (hg : Q.IsScSmoothOn S g U') (hf : P.IsScSmoothOn Q f U) (hfU : MapsTo f U U') :
    P.IsScSmoothOn S (g ∘ f) U where
  isOpen := hf.isOpen
  continuousOn := hg.continuousOn.comp hf.continuousOn hfU
  smooth φ χ hφ hχ V hV hVU hgfV := by
    have hVφ : V ⊆ φ.source := fun x hx => (hVU hx).2
    have hVU' : V ⊆ U := fun x hx => (hVU hx).1
    refine IsScSmoothRetractMap.of_locally ?_ ?_
    · rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
      change χ (g (f (φ.symm (φ x)))) ∈ χ.model.O
      rw [φ.symm_apply_apply (hVφ hx)]
      exact χ.mapsTo_model _ (hgfV hx)
    rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    -- a chart `ψ` of `Y` around `f x`, and the open sets `V' ⊆ U'` and `V₀ ⊆ V`
    obtain ⟨ψ, hψ, hfxψ⟩ := Q.exists_isChart_mem_source (f x)
    set V' := U' ∩ ψ.source ∩ g ⁻¹' χ.source with hV'
    have hV'o : IsOpen V' := by
      have : ContinuousOn g (U' ∩ ψ.source) := hg.continuousOn.mono inter_subset_left
      exact this.isOpen_inter_preimage (hg.isOpen.inter ψ.isOpen_source) χ.isOpen_source
    set V₀ := V ∩ f ⁻¹' V' with hV₀
    have hV₀o : IsOpen V₀ :=
      (hf.continuousOn.mono hVU').isOpen_inter_preimage hV hV'o
    have hxV₀ : x ∈ V₀ := ⟨hx, ⟨hfU (hVU' hx), hfxψ⟩, hgfV hx⟩
    have hV₀V : V₀ ⊆ V := inter_subset_left
    obtain ⟨W, hW, hWeq⟩ := φ.exists_isOpen_image_eq (hV₀V.trans hVφ) hV₀o
    refine ⟨W, hW, ?_, ?_⟩
    · have : φ x ∈ φ '' V₀ := ⟨x, hxV₀, rfl⟩
      rw [hWeq] at this; exact this.2
    · have hover : φ '' V ∩ W = φ '' V₀ := by
        rw [hWeq]
        ext z
        constructor
        · rintro ⟨hz, hzW⟩
          exact ⟨φ.image_subset_model hVφ hz, hzW⟩
        · rintro ⟨hz, hzW⟩
          refine ⟨?_, hzW⟩
          have : z ∈ φ '' V₀ := by rw [hWeq]; exact ⟨hz, hzW⟩
          exact image_mono hV₀V this
      rw [hover]
      -- the two factors
      have h1 : IsScSmoothRetractMap φ.model.E φ.model.C (φ '' V₀) ψ.model.E ψ.model.C (ψ '' V')
          (ψ ∘ f ∘ φ.symm) := by
        refine (hf.smooth φ ψ hφ hψ V₀ hV₀o (fun y hy => ⟨hVU' (hV₀V hy), hVφ (hV₀V hy)⟩)
          fun y hy => hy.2.1.2).mono_target ?_
        rintro _ ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
        change ψ (f (φ.symm (φ y))) ∈ ψ '' V'
        rw [φ.symm_apply_apply (hVφ (hV₀V hy))]
        exact ⟨f y, hy.2, rfl⟩
      have h2 : IsScSmoothRetractMap ψ.model.E ψ.model.C (ψ '' V') χ.model.E χ.model.C χ.model.O
          (χ ∘ g ∘ ψ.symm) :=
        hg.smooth ψ χ hψ hχ V' hV'o (fun y hy => ⟨hy.1.1, hy.1.2⟩) fun y hy => hy.2
      have hψV' : IsScRetract ψ.model.E ψ.model.C (ψ '' V') :=
        ψ.isScRetract_image (fun y hy => hy.1.2) hV'o
      refine (h2.comp h1 hψV').congr ?_
      rintro _ ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
      simp only [Function.comp_apply, φ.symm_apply_apply (hVφ (hV₀V hy)),
        ψ.symm_apply_apply hy.2.1.2]

theorem IsScSmoothMap.comp {f : X → Y} {g : Y → Z} (hg : Q.IsScSmoothMap S g)
    (hf : P.IsScSmoothMap Q f) : P.IsScSmoothMap S (g ∘ f) :=
  IsScSmoothOn.comp hg hf (mapsTo_univ _ _)

/-! ### Sub-M-polyfolds (Definition 2.3.18 (preprint 2.20)) -/

variable (P) in
/-- **Definition 2.3.18 (preprint 2.20)**: `A ⊆ X` is a **sub-M-polyfold** if every `a ∈ A` has an open neighbourhood
`V` and an sc-smooth retraction `r : V → V` (sc-smooth on `V`, `r ∘ r = r` on `V`) with
`r(V) = A ∩ V`. -/
def IsSubMPolyfold (A : Set X) : Prop :=
  ∀ a ∈ A, ∃ V : Set X, IsOpen V ∧ a ∈ V ∧ ∃ r : X → X, MapsTo r V V ∧ P.IsScSmoothOn P r V ∧
    (∀ x ∈ V, r (r x) = r x) ∧ r '' V = A ∩ V

/-- `X` is a sub-M-polyfold of itself (`r = id`). -/
lemma isSubMPolyfold_univ : P.IsSubMPolyfold univ := fun a _ =>
  ⟨univ, isOpen_univ, mem_univ a, id, mapsTo_id _, isScSmoothMap_id, fun _ _ => rfl, by simp⟩

end MPolyfold

/-! ### A retract as an M-polyfold -/

namespace LocalModel

variable (M : LocalModel)

open scoped Classical in
/-- The identity chart of a nonempty retract `O`, as a chart on the subtype `↥O`. -/
def selfChart (hO : M.O.Nonempty) : MChart M.O where
  model := M
  toPartialEquiv :=
    { toFun := Subtype.val
      invFun := fun z => if h : z ∈ M.O then ⟨z, h⟩ else ⟨hO.some, hO.some_mem⟩
      source := univ
      target := M.O
      map_source' := fun x _ => x.2
      map_target' := fun _ _ => mem_univ _
      left_inv' := fun x _ => by simp [x.2]
      right_inv' := fun z hz => by simp [hz] }
  isOpen_source := isOpen_univ
  target_eq := rfl
  continuousOn_toFun := continuous_subtype_val.continuousOn
  continuousOn_invFun := by
    refine continuousOn_iff_continuous_domRestrict.2 ?_
    have : (fun z : M.O => (if h : (z : M.E 0) ∈ M.O then (⟨z, h⟩ : M.O) else
        ⟨hO.some, hO.some_mem⟩)) = id := funext fun z => by simp [z.2]
    change Continuous (fun z : M.O => if h : (z : M.E 0) ∈ M.O then (⟨z, h⟩ : M.O) else
      ⟨hO.some, hO.some_mem⟩)
    rw [this]; exact continuous_id

lemma selfChart_apply (hO : M.O.Nonempty) (x : M.O) :
    (M.selfChart hO x : (M.selfChart hO).model.E 0) = (x : M.E 0) := rfl

lemma selfChart_source (hO : M.O.Nonempty) : (M.selfChart hO).source = univ := rfl

/-- A nonempty sc-smooth retract `(O, C, E)` is an M-polyfold, with the single chart
`id : O → O` (the text before Theorem 2.4.12 (preprint 2.31): "a sc-smooth retract `O` is a M-polyfold"). -/
def toMPolyfold (hO : M.O.Nonempty) : MPolyfold M.O where
  atlas :=
    { charts := {M.selfChart hO}
      compatible := fun φ hφ ψ hψ => by
        rw [mem_singleton_iff.1 hφ, mem_singleton_iff.1 hψ]
        exact MChart.compatible_self _
      cover := fun x => ⟨M.selfChart hO, mem_singleton _, mem_univ x⟩ }

/-- The M-polyfold of a relatively open subset `U` of a partial quadrant (the text's `X_C`). -/
def _root_.Polyfold.IsRelOpenInQuadrant.toMPolyfold {E : ScBanach} {C U : Set (E 0)}
    (hU : IsRelOpenInQuadrant E C U) (hne : U.Nonempty) : MPolyfold U :=
  (LocalModel.ofRelOpen hU).toMPolyfold hne

end LocalModel

end Polyfold
